## PROM-UM

PROM-UM is a validated patient-reported outcome measure for adults treated with plaque brachytherapy for uveal melanoma. It measures post-treatment Symptom Impairment, Worry, and Discomfort. The PROM-UM page includes information about the instrument, evidence base, licensing, USD fee categories, registration, and citation requirements.

Development evidence: Kopp BC, Crump RT, Weis E. The use of semistructured interviews to assess quality of life impacts for patients with uveal melanoma. Canadian Journal of Ophthalmology. 2017. doi:10.1016/j.jcjo.2016.10.005

Validation evidence: Weis E, Jiang J, Skalet AH, Shields CL, Crump RT. Psychometric Results of a New Patient-Reported Outcome Measure for Uveal Melanoma Post-Brachytherapy Treatment: The PROM-UM. Cancers. 2023;15:4142. doi:10.3390/cancers15164142

The 2017 qualitative study identified patient-important issues not fully captured by existing ophthalmic oncology quality-of-life tools, including mental health, family impact, travel and financial burden, and work and home life. The 2023 psychometric study evaluated PROM-UM in 439 patients from three North American ocular oncology centres and identified three domains: Symptom Impairment, Worry, and Discomfort.

PROM-UM licensing categories include academic/non-profit use, clinical use, and commercial or clinical trial use. Users should register before using, reproducing, distributing, translating, adapting, or electronically implementing PROM-UM.

